{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.35,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U7"],
      "pins": ["U7.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(U7-EN-Pad2)"],
      "observed": "U7 is the TPS62933 24 V to 5 V buck regulator. Its EN pin (pin 2) has no net and is marked no_connect. Every other control pin of U7 (RT, SS, FB, BST, VIN, SW, GND) is wired.",
      "expected": "The enable pin of a buck regulator should be tied to a defined level (for example to VIN through a divider, or to a pull-up or pull-down) so the converter starts reliably. A floating EN can leave the +5V rail unpowered or make start-up unpredictable.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"2\") ...) absent; (net (code \"143\") (name \"unconnected-(U7-EN-Pad2)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U7\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"EN\") (pintype \"input+no_connect\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(libpart ... \"REG ADJ 3A BUCK TPS62933 SOT583\" ... (pin (num \"2\") (name \"EN\") (type \"input\")))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "U1 — TPS62933 (TI) | 24 V → 5 V synchronous buck regulator, 3 A"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the EN pin has no internal pull-up in this part, the 5 V rail (which powers the ESP32 DevKit and the 3V3 LDO) may never start, or may start intermittently. The whole board would then be non-functional.",
      "confidence": 0.35
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist and SPICE deck agree on values and most connectivity, and the isolator, sense-resistor and feedback networks look consistent. The one candidate deviation is the TPS62933 enable pin left unconnected, which is only a problem if the part has no internal pull, so confidence is moderate."
}

